 refers to Arthur as her  master and she vows to protect him even  if it costs her her life the final page  according to some translations reads  without seeking for their understanding  and nor their help  the witch carries on a new sin van this  chapter was weird and it raises so many  questions what exactly is this new sin  that the witch is carrying is it  referring to something bad that she did  or is about to do or is this tried  tell us that Arthur will literally  become a new member of the seven deadly  sins and replace Eskin or on top of that  why's Marilyn calling Arthur her master  when she has been his mentor this whole  time and when he is so much younger and  less experienced than her  I guess Merlin might just be committed  to serving the king of chaos but if so  what exactly does she need to protect  Arthur from by the looks of it cath is  completely destroyed unless the monster  can regenerate or something along those  lines and we know that the demon king  has been defeated so who else could  possibly challenge the king of chaos the  obvious answer is of course the supreme  deity but she has been ignored for so  long and the story that talking about  her until we get some concrete  information about her seems like a waste  of time at this point  also if Kath has really been defeated by  just a single cut from Arthur's sword  then what was the point of this big calf  twist in the first place  why have Kath transform and attacked the  sins only to have the same creature  one-shotted in the very next chapter in  my previous seven deadly sins video I  speculated it Kath may have a bigger  role to play in all of this and that  perhaps Kath will somehow connected to  the goddesses and the supreme deity it  now seems that Kath is connected to the  goddesses in the sense that they were  the ones who had sealed it away and so  perhaps the goddesses were the ones who  decided to release Kath again when the  right time came but other than that I am  really no